.TH CWE-321 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-321 \- Use of Hard\-coded Cryptographic Key
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The use of a hard\-coded cryptographic key significantly increases the possibility that encrypted data may be recovered.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2025\-30406
Gladinet CentreStack, added 2025\-04\-08.
.PP
Gladinet CentreStack and Triofox Use of Hard\-coded Cryptographic Key Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Gladinet CentreStack and Triofox contains a use of hard\-coded cryptographic key vulnerability in the way that the application manages keys used for ViewState integrity verification. Successful exploitation allows an attacker to forge ViewState payloads for server\-side deserialization, allowing for remote code execution.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2025\-04\-29.
.PP
